    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Seiya Suzuki** (67.36) and **Corbin Carroll** (64.88) headline our production expectations. **Seiya Suzuki** draws a favorable matchup against Seth Lugo, benefiting from an SP xERA of 4.66 and a significant +16% boost from the opposing pitcher's skill profile, while **Corbin Carroll** remains a must-start despite the presence of Yoshinobu Yamamoto; **Corbin Carroll**\u2019s elite speed profile and the +8% boost from batting second provide the necessary ceiling in a high-variance matchup. **Brice Turang** (64.10) and **Isaac Paredes** (64.27) also offer strong returns, with **Brice Turang** capitalizing on a prime lead-off spot and a favorable stolen base environment against a slower delivery, while **Isaac Paredes** exploits a mid-tier arm in King to provide solid stability at the 1B spot.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the board was the exclusion of **Cole Young**, who sat at a 39.56 efficiency score. While his potential order placement at #2 was enticing, the optimizer penalized his projected output due to the high-skill arm of Griffin Jax and unfavorable park factors, ultimately leading us to favor the established volume of **Josh Naylor** (51.02) and the efficiency of our OF core. We are keeping a close watch on **Max Muncy** (62.89) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (60.58), both of whom are buoyed by a +5% wind-out factor in their matchup against Bennett. While **Max Muncy**\u2019s #8 spot in the lineup is a drag on his overall profile, his platoon advantage and stolen base opportunity against a slow-working pitcher keep him firmly in the \"Strong\" start category. \n\nRisks remain present across the board, particularly for **Gabriel Moreno** (53.37) and **Austin Riley** (51.01), both of whom face high-tier arms in Yamamoto and Cole, respectively. We are operating with a cautious eye on **Zach McKinstry** (42.77); his marginal score is heavily hampered by his #9 lineup position and a negative platoon shift, meaning he is on a short leash to preserve our daily game caps. While we continue to navigate the absence of **James Wood** and **Giancarlo Stanton** due to IL stints, the focus for the day remains on maximizing the SB potential of **Brice Turang**, **Corbin Carroll**, and **Jose Caballero** to close the gap in our scarcest category.",
